content.text:
## ChatKit Studio — 2025 dark-mode chat UI direction

A polished ChatKit Studio interface should feel **quiet, dense, and system-native** rather than like a conventional “colored bubble” messenger.

### 1. Layout

```text
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  ☰   Workspace / Assistant        GPT-4.1 ▾  │
├───────────────┬──────────────────────────────┤
│ Threads       │                              │
│               │       Conversation           │
│ + New chat    │                              │
│ Today         │  assistant message           │
│  Project plan │                              │
│  Untitled     │                 user message │
│               │                              │
│ Yesterday     │                              │
│  Research     │                              │
│               │                              │
│               ├──────────────────────────────┤
│               │  +  Ask anything…       ↑    │
└───────────────┴──────────────────────────────┘
```

Recommended proportions:

- **Sidebar:** 240–280 px on desktop
- **Chat content:** max-width 720–800 px
- **Composer:** max-width 720 px, sticky to bottom
- **Message spacing:** 20–28 px between message groups
- **Mobile:** collapse the sidebar into a menu button

ChatKit supports built-in history, thread management, attachments, widgets, and streaming, so the visual system can focus on hierarchy rather than recreating those primitives. ([openai.github.io](https://openai.github.io/chatkit-js/?utm_source=openai))

---

## 2. Dark-mode color system

Avoid pure black and pure white. Use near-black surfaces with subtle elevation changes.

```css
:root {
  --bg: #0d0f12;
  --surface-1: #12151a;
  --surface-2: #181c22;
  --surface-3: #20252d;

  --border: #2a3039;
  --border-subtle: #20252d;

  --text-primary: #f2f4f7;
  --text-secondary: #a5adb9;
  --text-muted: #737d8b;

  --accent: #8ab4ff;
  --accent-strong: #5b91f5;
  --danger: #ff7b82;
  --success: #65d69a;

  --user-message: #242b35;
  --assistant-message: transparent;
  --input-bg: #171b21;
}
```

### Accessibility targets

- Primary text: at least **4.5:1** contrast
- Secondary text: avoid using below **4.5:1** for essential information
- Focus ring: 2 px accent color with a visible offset
- Do not communicate status through color alone
- Keep destructive actions visually distinct but not overly saturated

ChatKit’s theme configuration exposes color scheme, density, radius, typography, and color customization. Its documented color modes are `light` and `dark`; dark mode can be selected directly through `colorScheme: 'dark'`. ([openai.github.io](https://openai.github.io/chatkit-js/api/openai/chatkit-react/type-aliases/colorscheme/?utm_source=openai))

---

## 3. Message bubbles

### User messages

Use a restrained surface rather than a bright accent bubble:

```css
.message--user {
  max-width: 78%;
  margin-left: auto;
  padding: 10px 14px;
  color: var(--text-primary);
  background: var(--user-message);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 18px 18px 5px 18px;
}
```

### Assistant messages

Assistant messages should usually be **bubbleless** or use only a very subtle container:

```css
.message--assistant {
  max-width: 100%;
  padding: 4px 0;
  color: var(--text-primary);
  background: transparent;
}
```

Recommended treatment:

- User: contained bubble
- Assistant: open text block
- Tool result: bordered card
- Error: tinted red surface
- System notice: centered muted label
- Streaming response: preserve layout while text grows
- Code: separate elevated block with copy action

This gives the assistant response more readable width and avoids making long answers feel like text-message balloons.

### Message metadata

Keep metadata secondary:

```text
GPT-4.1 · 10:42 AM
```

Use 11–12 px text, muted color, and reveal detailed controls on hover or focus:

- Copy
- Retry
- Edit
- More
- Branch / continue
- Feedback

---

## 4. Model picker

Place the model picker in the header, aligned right:

```text
[ GPT-4.1 ▾ ]
```

The closed state should show:

- Model name
- Optional capability indicator
- Chevron
- Current status, if loading or unavailable

Example menu:

```text
GPT-4.1
Strong reasoning and coding
────────────────────────
GPT-4o
Fast multimodal responses

o3
Deep reasoning

Auto
Choose automatically
```

Use a compact popover:

```css
.model-picker {
  min-width: 240px;
  padding: 6px;
  background: var(--surface-2);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 16px 40px rgb(0 0 0 / 35%);
}

.model-option {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
  gap: 4px 12px;
  padding: 10px 12px;
  border-radius: 8px;
}

.model-option:hover,
.model-option[aria-selected="true"] {
  background: var(--surface-3);
}
```

Important implementation detail: OpenAI’s current ChatKit documentation lists the **model picker as supported for self-hosted ChatKit backends**, while the OpenAI-hosted backend feature list does not include it. If the picker is a product requirement, plan on a self-hosted ChatKit runtime or implement model switching outside the hosted configuration. ([openai.github.io](https://openai.github.io/chatkit-js/?utm_source=openai))

---

## 5. Composer

Use a single elevated composer rather than a permanently visible toolbar.

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Ask anything…                                │
│  ＋ Attach    / Tools                         ↑ │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

States:

1. **Empty:** placeholder and attachment button
2. **Typing:** send button becomes active
3. **Streaming:** send button changes to stop
4. **Attachment added:** attachment chips appear above the text
5. **Tool selected:** tool badge appears inside the composer
6. **Error:** inline retry state, not a blocking modal

Suggested styling:

```css
.composer {
  padding: 10px;
  background: var(--input-bg);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 20px;
  box-shadow: 0 8px 28px rgb(0 0 0 / 22%);
}

.composer:focus-within {
  border-color: var(--accent-strong);
  box-shadow:
    0 0 0 2px rgb(91 145 245 / 25%),
    0 8px 28px rgb(0 0 0 / 22%);
}
```

ChatKit exposes composer configuration through the `composer` option and supports attachments and tool-related UI in the broader component system. ([openai.github.io](https://openai.github.io/chatkit-js/api/openai/chatkit-react/type-aliases/chatkitoptions/?utm_source=openai))

---

## 6. Recommended visual tokens

| Token | Recommendation |
|---|---:|
| Base radius | 10–12 px |
| Composer radius | 18–22 px |
| Button radius | 8–10 px |
| User bubble radius | 18 px, asymmetric corner |
| Default density | Normal |
| Compact density | Dense admin or developer tools |
| Content width | 720–800 px |
| Body text | 15–16 px |
| Metadata | 11–12 px |
| Code text | 13–14 px |
| Border opacity | Subtle, never pure gray |
| Animation | 120–180 ms ease-out |

ChatKit officially supports `compact`, `normal`, and `spacious` density modes, plus `pill`, `round`, `soft`, and `sharp` radius modes. For this visual direction, `normal` density with `soft` or `round` corners is a good starting point. ([openai.github.io](https://openai.github.io/chatkit-js/api/openai/chatkit/type-aliases/themeoption/?utm_source=openai))

---

## 7. ChatKit configuration example

```tsx
import { ChatKit, useChatKit } from "@openai/chatkit-react";

export function DarkChat() {
  const { control } = useChatKit({
    api: {
      url: "/api/chatkit",
      domainKey: "my-app",
    },

    theme: {
      colorScheme: "dark",
      density: "normal",
      radius: "soft",

      color: {
        grayscale: {
          hue: 220,
          tint: 1,
          shade: 0,
        },
        accent: {
          primary: "#8ab4ff",
          level: 2,
        },
      },
    },

    header: {
      enabled: true,
    },

    composer: {
      placeholder: "Ask anything…",
    },

    frameTitle: "AI assistant",
  });

  return (
    <ChatKit
      control={control}
      className="h-screen w-full bg-[#0d0f12]"
    />
  );
}
```

The documented ChatKit options include `theme`, `composer`, `header`, `history`, `thread`, `widgets`, and `threadItemActions`. ([openai.github.io](https://openai.github.io/chatkit-js/api/openai/chatkit-react/type-aliases/chatkitoptions/?utm_source=openai))

### Suggested design principle

**Use color to express state, not identity.**

The model picker, user bubble, tool results, and action buttons should share a restrained accent system. The primary visual distinction should come from spacing, surface elevation, and typography—not from a different bright color for every message type.

## Sources
5 sources
[1] https://platform.openai.com/docs/quickstart/make-your-first-api-request
    https://platform.openai.com/docs/quickstart/make-your-first-api-request
[2] https://community.openai.com/t/found-a-problem-where-the-message-window-appears-white-in-dark-mode/1205945
    https://community.openai.com/t/found-a-problem-where-the-message-window-appears-white-in-dark-mode/1205945
[3] https://community.openai.com/t/chatkit-not-displaying-any-messages-when-using-customapiconfig-ndjson-streaming-deltas-received-but-not-rendered/1366591
    https://community.openai.com/t/chatkit-not-displaying-any-messages-when-using-customapiconfig-ndjson-streaming-deltas-received-but-not-rendered/1366591
[4] https://cdn.openai.com/business-guides-and-resources/ai-in-the-enterprise.pdf
    https://cdn.openai.com/business-guides-and-resources/ai-in-the-enterprise.pdf
[5] https://cdn.openai.com/threat-intelligence-reports/5f73af09-a3a3-4a55-992e-069237681620/disrupting-malicious-uses-of-ai-june-2025.pdf?trk=public_post_comment-text
