expo-font is installed but expo-splash-screen is not. I can use expo-font's useFonts without SplashScreen (just gate rendering on font load). Actually the standard pattern uses SplashScreen.preventAutoHideAsync, but I can do it without splash screen by just rendering a loading view until fonts load, or by using useFonts and conditionally rendering.

Actually, in Expo, @expo/vector-icons fonts ARE bundled and load automatically in most cases. But in a dev client build (expo run:android), sometimes they need explicit loading. The cleanest root fix: use useFonts(Ionicons.font) at app root and gate the app render until loaded.

Let me implement in App.tsx:
```tsx
import { useFonts } from 'expo-font';
import { Ionicons } from '@expo/vector-icons';

export default function App() {
  const [fontsLoaded] = useFonts(Ionicons.font);
  const { hydrate } = useStore();
  useEffect(() => { hydrate(); }, []);
  if (!fontsLoaded) return null; // or a loading view
  return (...);
}
```

This guarantees Ionicons font is loaded before rendering any screen. Then revert HomeScreen glyph swap back to Ionicons.

