const [kbHeight, setKbHeight] = useState(0);
useEffect(() => {
  const show = Keyboard.addListener('keyboardDidShow', (e) => setKbHeight(e.endCoordinates.height));
  const hide = Keyboard.addListener('keyboardDidHide', () => setKbHeight(0));
  return () => { show.remove(); hide.remove(); };
}, []);
Composer wrapper: <View style={{ paddingBottom: kbHeight > 0 ? kbHeight : insets.bottom }}> around ChatInput? ChatInput already receives a bottomInset prop = insets.bottom. Change: pass bottomInset={kbHeight > 0 ? kbHeight : insets.bottom}. But the composer needs to move up: the composer is at the bottom of the column; adding paddingBottom to the container pushes it up ✓. Also, so the list can use the space: KAV previously resized the whole column; with padding on the outer container, the list shrinks too ✓ (container is flex column: topbar, list flex1, input; padding at the bottom of the container shrinks the available area ✓).

Glitch where it doesn't come back down: keyboardDidHide sets 0 ✓ deterministic.

W2b collapse glitch: in MessageList, when liveOpen toggles during generation: after toggle, scrollToEnd without animation: inside the toggle handler: requestAnimationFrame(() => flatList.scrollToEnd({animated:false})). Find the liveOpen toggle in MessageList.

